Subject: Fix: shots no longer pass through the goalies after a cut-short deke (issue #38)
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A fix of the original game, always on and without a switch (owner decision,
2026-10-12). It lives in the tweak series so the faithful series stays retail.

The NK ("No Kritter") bug, or Boo glitch: a fielder who turns intangible while
he carries the ball (Boo's deke and Skillshot, the teleport dekes of Waluigi,
Daisy and Dry Bones, Monty Mole and Yoshi, a Peach photo) also switches off the
ball's collisions with players and goalies (cFielder::SetTangible). Turning
tangible again switches them back on only if he still carries the ball. If he
loses it while intangible they stay off: the ball goes through the players and
through both goalies, whose contacts and through-goalie check need them, so
every shot and chip on goal scores. That lasts until the next kickoff
(ResetBall), the end of a Skillshot or Mega Strike, or another intangible
carrier who still has the ball when he turns tangible (another Boo deke). The
original code does the same.

The known triggers: Boo dekes next to his own goalie with the ball. The goalie
takes the ball from a teammate who hoards it beside him
(Goalie::IsTeammateHoardingBall, ActionGrabBall) without checking that he is
intangible, and the steal ends Boo's deke without the ball. A teleport deke ends
in a goal: the deker is lifted above it, to be electrocuted on the fence, and
the ball is dropped in front of the goal line. Or a Chain Chomp lands on a
deking ball carrier: while it arrives (CHAIN_STATE_RECOVER) it hits players
whether or not they are intangible, and cFielder::CollideWithChainCallback
knocks the ball loose.

cPlayer::ReleaseBall now gives a ball released by an intangible fielder its
player and goalie collisions back, as it already gives back its visibility.
That covers every way an intangible carrier loses the ball. The dekes, the
goalie's grab and the Chain Chomp's hit stay as in the original game; only the
ball keeps colliding with the goalies afterwards. Boo's and Monty Mole's
Skillshots and Mega Strikes, which keep the ball off the goalie on purpose, are
unchanged: they switch the collisions off after the shot's release, or the
shooter is tangible when he shoots.

diff --git a/src/Game/Player.cpp b/src/Game/Player.cpp
index c5230fd..ab457f8 100644
--- a/src/Game/Player.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Player.cpp
@@ -827,6 +827,21 @@ void cPlayer::ReleaseBall(int nParam)
     {
         g_pBall->m_bVisible = true;
     }
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port fix, always on (issue #38, the NK bug): a fielder who turns
+    // intangible while carrying the ball switches off the ball's player and
+    // goalie collisions too (cFielder::SetTangible), and only switches them
+    // back on if he still carries it when he turns tangible again. A fielder
+    // who loses the ball while intangible (his own goalie taking it from a
+    // deking Boo, a teleport deke ending above a goal) left them off, and the
+    // ball went through both goalies until the next kickoff. As with its
+    // visibility above, the released ball gets them back.
+    if (m_eClassType == FIELDER && !((cFielder*)this)->mbTangible)
+    {
+        g_pBall->m_pPhysicsBall->mbCanCollidePlayer = true;
+        g_pBall->m_pPhysicsBall->mbCanCollideGoalie = true;
+    }
+#endif
 }
 
 void StartPlayerFire(cPlayer* pPlayer, float fDuration)
